    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges (structural impact kept low \u2014 new behaviour added as a small, self-contained unit rather than growing an existing method/class):\n\n1. **`OwnerTimezonePolicy.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny standalone policy class mirroring the existing `OwnerLocalityPolicy`. Its single `timezone(owner)` method looks up the region (via `OwnerLocalityPolicy.locality`) in an immutable `NSW/VIC/QLD \u2192 IANA` map, returning `null` when unmapped. No surrounding complexity to hold.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line delegating `timezone` to the new policy, matching the established pattern for all the other derived fields.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW` \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
